; A value assembled from loads with or/shl/zext is also tested on bits that
; come from only some of the loads. The parts may also be joined with 'add',
; which InstCombine turns into 'or' because the parts do not overlap.
; Narrowing the test onto part of the tree (an inner 'or', 'shl' or 'zext')
; gives that part a second use, which stops the loads from being combined
; into one wide load, so the test must stay on the full value. When the full
; value cannot be combined anyway (a leaf is not a load, the loads use
; different bases, or part of the tree already has another use), the test may
; be narrowed, but only down to the largest part that can still be combined.

